{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Lesson 4 — Loan Portfolio SQL Exploration\n",
        "\n",
        "**Portfolio:** Loan Portfolio Performance & Risk Analytics  \n",
        "**Tools:** Google Colab + DuckDB SQL  \n",
        "**Analysis snapshot:** 2026-08-31  \n",
        "**Currency:** IDR\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook uses **fictional/synthetic** CSV files, not confidential employer data.\n",
        "\n",
        
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1 — Install and import the SQL engine\n",
        "\n",
        "DuckDB is a SQL analytics engine. You will write SQL; we use a few short Python lines only to set up the connection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%pip -q install duckdb\n",
        "import duckdb\n",
        "print(\"DuckDB is ready:\", duckdb.__version__)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2 — Upload the five CSVs\n",
        "\n",
        "Click **Choose Files** below. Select all five CSVs from your computer. Do not upload your old employer data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from google.colab import files\n",
        "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
        "required = {\"borrowers.csv\", \"lenders.csv\", \"loans.csv\", \"installments.csv\", \"repayments.csv\"}\n",
        "missing = required - set(uploaded)\n",
        "if missing:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(f\"Missing files: {sorted(missing)}. Run this cell again and upload all five CSVs.\")\n",
        "print(\"All five dataset files uploaded successfully.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3 — Create SQL views\n",
        "\n",
        "A **view** is a SQL table-like object that reads data from the CSV. Views here live only in this Colab session."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "con = duckdb.connect(database=\":memory:\")\n",
        "for name in [\"borrowers\", \"lenders\", \"loans\", \"installments\", \"repayments\"]:\n",
        "    con.execute(f\"CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW {name} AS SELECT * FROM read_csv_auto('{name}.csv')\")\n",
        "print(\"SQL views ready: borrowers, lenders, loans, installments, repayments\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4 — Preview the raw loan data\n",
        "\n",
        "`SELECT *` means all columns; `LIMIT 5` keeps the output short."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "con.sql(\"\"\"\n",
        "SELECT *\n",
        "FROM loans\n",
        "LIMIT 5;\n",
        "\"\"\").df()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5 — Check how many rows each table contains\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected row counts: borrowers 1,500; lenders 4; loans 2,000; installments 19,458; repayments 13,641."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "con.sql(\"\"\"\n",
        "SELECT 'borrowers' AS table_name, COUNT(*) AS total_rows FROM borrowers\n",
        "UNION ALL\n",
        "SELECT 'lenders', COUNT(*) FROM lenders\n",
        "UNION ALL\n",
        "SELECT 'loans', COUNT(*) FROM loans\n",
        "UNION ALL\n",
        "SELECT 'installments', COUNT(*) FROM installments\n",
        "UNION ALL\n",
        "SELECT 'repayments', COUNT(*) FROM repayments;\n",
        "\"\"\").df()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6 — Business question: Which lending partner disbursed the most principal?\n",
        "\n",
        "This uses a `JOIN` to translate lender IDs into lender names, and `GROUP BY` to aggregate loans. It calculates **historical cumulative disbursement**, not current outstanding principal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "con.sql(\"\"\"\n",
        "SELECT\n",
        "    ld.lender_name,\n",
        "    COUNT(*) AS total_loans,\n",
        "    SUM(l.principal_amount) AS total_disbursement_idr,\n",
        "    ROUND(AVG(l.principal_amount), 0) AS avg_loan_size_idr\n",
        "FROM loans AS l\n",
        "JOIN lenders AS ld\n",
        "    ON l.lender_id = ld.lender_id\n",
        "WHERE CAST(l.disbursement_date AS DATE) <= DATE '2026-08-31'\n",
        "GROUP BY ld.lender_name\n",
        "ORDER BY total_disbursement_idr DESC;\n",
        "\"\"\").df()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7 — Business question: How did monthly disbursement change?\n",
        "\n",
        "The `DATE_TRUNC` function groups disbursement dates into calendar months."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "con.sql(\"\"\"\n",
        "SELECT\n",
        "    DATE_TRUNC('month', CAST(disbursement_date AS DATE)) AS disbursement_month,\n",
        "    COUNT(*) AS loan_count,\n",
        "    SUM(principal_amount) AS disbursement_idr\n",
        "FROM loans\n",
        "WHERE CAST(disbursement_date AS DATE) <= DATE '2026-08-31'\n",
        "GROUP BY 1\n",
        "ORDER BY 1;\n",
        "\"\"\").df()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8 — Data quality: find missing borrower or lender references\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected results: 0 and 0. If the results are not zero, investigate before making a dashboard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "con.sql(\"\"\"\n",
        "SELECT\n",
        "  SUM(CASE WHEN b.borrower_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS loans_without_borrower,\n",
        "  SUM(CASE WHEN ld.lender_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS loans_without_lender\n",
        "FROM loans AS l\n",
        "LEFT JOIN borrowers AS b ON l.borrower_id = b.borrower_id\n",
        "LEFT JOIN lenders AS ld ON l.lender_id = ld.lender_id;\n",
        "\"\"\").df()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9 — Important: Avoid a misleading JOIN\n",
        "\n",
        "Joining `loans` directly to `repayments` and then summing `loans.principal_amount` **overcounts** disbursements when one loan has multiple repayments. In later lessons we'll aggregate repayments at loan level *before* joining to loans.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Your mission:** Interpret your lender ranking and monthly trend in 2–3 sentences in English. Do not infer the real-world behavior of borrowers from this synthetic dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Next lesson:** Define and calculate outstanding principal, overdue amounts and DPD as of 2026-08-31."
      ]
    }
